        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(infra): drop replacement characters when response snippets truncate UTF-8",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users could see replacement characters in bounded web/provider error snippets when a response body was truncated in the middle of a multi-byte UTF-8 character.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe bounded response readers now use streaming decode only for truncated byte prefixes, so incomplete trailing UTF-8 sequences are omitted instead of rendered as U+FFFD. The change keeps the normal full-response decode path flushing normally, and uses a fresh UTF-8 fallback decoder so unsupported charset fallback cannot retain streaming state between responses.\n\n## User Impact\n\nProvider error details and web_fetch snippets remain clean and readable when OpenClaw caps large response bodies at a byte boundary.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: bounded response text helpers drop partial UTF-8 characters when stream reads stop at maxBytes, while preserving clean fallback charset decoding between responses.\n- Current-head proof at 5d9ef2ab883ab8e51b587fa6b929347c91d15176: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/http-error-body.test.ts src/agents/tools/web-shared.test.ts` passed 2 Vitest shards / 31 tests.\n- PR diff hygiene: `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Review proof: `python .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main` passed with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Duplicate search: no open or closed OpenClaw PRs found for the bounded response UTF-8 truncation / replacement-character issue.",
